From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 09:02:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: scm: add QSEECOM app loading and listener
 services
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add the SCM calls the QSEECOM TEE driver needs to bring a trusted
application up from Linux and to answer the file-storage requests it
makes while it runs: app load (QSEE_OS/APP_MGR/APP_START, the image
handed over as one TZ-memory blob), app shutdown, and listener
register/deregister/response.

A QSEECOM call that comes back INCOMPLETE naming a listener is serviced
and resumed under the existing call lock until the application
finishes, with a bounded number of rounds so that a misbehaving
application cannot hold the lock for ever. An unknown listener id is
still answered, with a failure, because leaving the request unanswered
parks the application in TZ and makes every later QSEECOM call return
-EBUSY until the device is power cycled.

All behavioural changes to the shared call path are gated on
CONFIG_TEE_QSEECOM. Without it, qcom_scm_qseecom_call() keeps its
previous lock scope and its WARN_ON()s for incomplete and blocked
calls, listener registration is refused with -EOPNOTSUPP, and no TEE
device is registered; the new exported helpers are present but have no
caller. With it, the TEE platform device is registered ahead of the
in-kernel client allowlist, deliberately: the allowlist gates clients
that attach to applications during probe, whereas the TEE front-end is
opt-in at build time and does nothing until user space opens it.

The SCM code is the QSEECOM TEE RFC by Dawid Wróbel, unchanged apart
from the CONFIG_TEE_QSEECOM gating and the restored blank lines that the
first import had removed from unrelated functions. Dawid Wróbel's
copyright line is retained.

Co-developed-by: Dawid Wróbel <me@dawidwrobel.com>
Based-on: https://github.com/wrobelda/linux/tree/qcom-qseecom-tee
  (5dbfe45eb45c, 4ed582034125, e511d21adc14, 8405dec9eca0, ac278d7fa277,
  e101f59d65c2, 80d0fbd009d0)
Based-on: https://github.com/yzddmr6/linux-sm8450-liuqin/pull/7 (yuzelingsha)
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

